^warning: ignoring
--
`D t = D{{6}, 7};' leaves t with wrong members (assertion 2 fails), although
`D d{{6}, 7};' is right: the trace shows the prvalue's temporary with w = 6,
so the braced list of the explicit type conversion ([expr.type.conv]/2) is
matched to the members without the base element. The same prvalue thrown as
an exception gives a wrong exception object. Found while working on the
lifetime of exception objects; also with W184 (before that work).
